WEBVTT

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.330
Yasaka-kun!

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:23.460
Arashi-san.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.910
You're going to fight, no matter what?

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:33.320
There are times when a man must fight, even when he knows he'll lose.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:36.670
Goodbye, Arashi-san.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:38.120
Wait, Yasaka-kun!

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:38.800
Don't go.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.930
Why? Why do all this?

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:47.590
This planet's fate has nothing to do with you.

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:51.620
But you've suffered and been hurt so much.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.520
Why put yourself through all this to fight?

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:59.200
Maybe... Maybe it's because I wanted to see your smile.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:03.480
If I come back alive, I'll...

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:07.180
If I come back alive...

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.300
Wait a second.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.050
"Come back"... "Come back"...

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:17.270
How do I write the kanji for "come back" again?

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.140
This isn't it.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:22.520
But it's close...

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.250
It's like this.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.390
Oh, I get it.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.640
What are you doing here, Arashi-san?!

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.400
You were so late, I came to get you.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.740
If you don't hurry, you'll be late to work at the Ark.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.950
Good morning, Hajime-chan.

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:17.760
This is how the city looked when I was alive.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.270
When you were alive?

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:20.550
Then...

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.170
Yes.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.050
I am a ghost.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:25.930
Ghost?

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:32.540
I Want to Protect Her

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.400
But I can sure feel her...

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:44.450
Hajime-chan, what were you writing this morning?

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:45.290
Huh?

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.810
Oh, that was a book report.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.420
Wow!

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:53.840
Well, it was a report at first,
but it turned into an original story.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.680
Hajime-chan, I didn't know you liked that stuff.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:01.550
In every era, man aspires to be a hero of justice.

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.290
A hero of justice?

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:07.280
A hero who risks his life fighting to protect humanity.

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:13.370
Oh, right! Want to go to the arcade today, after work?

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:14.280
Arcade?

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.800
You've never been to one before?

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:20.080
I've never moved much from this area.

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:23.600
Then let's go. I'll take you.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.420
OK, I'll try it.

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:31.850
Iced tea. With milk.

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:33.300
Me, too.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:34.850
All right.

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.530
You working here, too?

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:39.030
I was won in a bet.

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:41.220
Same with four-eyes over there.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.060
Don't call me four-eyes!

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.790
Master, two iced teas with milk.

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:46.850
Right!

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:50.740
Sure is nice to make money.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:56.580
Business has been slow lately, but I guess if you keep it up, things will work out.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:05:00.150
But they're almost all guys from the university.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.090
What's wrong with that?

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:09.840
Unspoiled boys, with love's soft flames igniting in their hearts, coming to see their favorite master.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.200
I'm such a naughty woman.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.270
A criminal, I'll give you that.

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:18.920
I doubt any of them are into girls with no brains, only tits.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.020
Um, pass the salt.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.700
What did you say, kid?

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.320
I'll jam coffee beans down your throat till you choke!

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:25.500
You wanna fight, old lady?

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:28.320
Who're you calling old?
Drop the last digit, and I'm 20!

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.220
Yeah, right!

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.310
Do your jobs already.

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:31.510
The salt, please.

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:34.170
They're obviously after Arashi-san.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:41.100
She <i>is</i> cute. Her hair's so pretty, and she has a pure, clean manner to her-

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:38.610
I've never seen you around here.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:39.820
That outfit looks good on you.

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:40.860
Thank you!

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:42.080
Of course!

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:43.540
Don't get all haughty about it.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:47.980
And that slightly vulnerable feel interests men...

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.880
Who cares about long black hair?

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:53.360
And if you want vulnerability, I've got it coming out my ass!

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:56.290
With you, it's a trap, not vulnerability.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.590
She's a pro con artist...

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:00.370
Hey, let's exchange cellphone email addresses.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:03.740
Cellphone email addresses

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:05.570
You don't have a cell?

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:08.750
I'm sorry. I'm not good with new things.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:11.970
Excuse me. Please pass the salt.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:16.310
My circle's got a drinking party tonight. Want to come?

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:19.090
Circle?

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:21.160
I'm sorry. I don't really understand.

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:23.480
The salt...

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:28.820
We're the home movie circle;
we were looking for a girl with black hair.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.990
You'd be perfect for it. Just perfect!

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:33.280
That sounds fun!

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:37.540
But I'm sorry. I have plans today.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:38.790
Aww.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.830
Next time, then. Make sure you come.

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:42.880
Um, pass the salt.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:45.830
Pathetic... You're just going to sit and watch?

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:48.870
Shut up! Arashi-san has the right to choose, you know.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:53.230
The way you give the other guy a chance really shows you're a kid.

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:56.310
Right. I'm putting her happiness above my own.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:59.640
It's almost identical to being a softie who lets his one chance escape.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:00.960
And hypocritical.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:06.400
If I can spend time with Arashi-san, right now, that's enough for me.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:10.170
If you're a man, you should know how I feel.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:12.700
Well, I do.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:15.540
But you don't have enough self-control.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:17.100
And you aren't worried enough.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:18.340
What do you mean?

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:21.630
Welcome!

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:25.890
Why is Arashi-san staying with you, is what I'm asking.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:31.460
Don't you think it's weird that a person you don't know suddenly wants to stay with you?

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:32.790
W-Well...

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:37.430
Being a nice guy is fine, but be careful.
There's more to women than meets the eye.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:38.680
More?

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.520
Women can be very calculating.

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:44.600
Any time they do something, they've thought it out.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:45.850
Shut up.

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:47.180
You're just jealous!

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:48.620
Like hell I am!

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:49.850
Stay in your little fantasy.

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:51.870
But don't blame me when you get hurt.

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:56.230
I'm sure Arashi-san would never do anything like that.

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:57.990
Of course, but...

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:10.550
Don't run away.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:11.830
Salt, please.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:24.870
Bye.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.220
Yeah. See ya.

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:29.840
Jun, wanna go to the arcade, too?

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:32.020
No, I've got something to do.

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:34.940
OK. Hop on, and I'll take you as far as the station.

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:37.620
You do have some good points.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:39.890
I'm a paragon of generosity and kindness.

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:42.520
Hey, Arashi-san, race you to the bottom.

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:44.000
Sure. I won't lose!

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:48.790
Get ready!

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:57.960
See you.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.280
I'll never ride with you again!

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:01.850
All right! Let's get going.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:02.930
OK!

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.600
This place sure has changed...

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:12.180
This is the arcade, Arashi-san.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:13.970
Amazing!

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:17.240
Look at this! All these dolls!

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:18.740
So cute...

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:21.150
She's finally noticed it, then?

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:24.710
It's the "crane game," the arcade's ultimate weapon.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:30.700
Its power is to steal your wallet's contents by making you think that you were <i>this close</i>

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:33.980
and you could get the prize with just <i>one more try!</i>

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:37.010
But they're so cute!

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:42.310
Many valiant soldiers have challenged the crane game, but none survived.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:45.180
I had no idea it was such a fearsome thing.

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:47.390
But they're so cute...

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:48.760
Don't underestimate the arcade.

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:51.230
I'll show you how it's done!

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:52.940
Yes, sir, Captain!

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:54.900
First, insert 100 yen!

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:56.530
Then press parallel move.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.440
Then perpendicular move.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.140
And then release the button at the right time!

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:11.780
Mission failed...

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:12.760
Captain!

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:17.320
Th-The enemy's defenses were stronger than anticipated.

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.760
Are you all right, Captain?

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:23.110
Forget about me. You must rescue him.

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:25.880
No, I can't leave you!

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:27.110
You idiot!

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:34.050
If you don't, then who's going to save him?

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:39.010
Roger. I'll save him, no matter the cost!

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:43.330
Go!

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:46.910
Listen, be sure to look carefully.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.430
The enemy has planted decoys.

00:10:48.430 --> 00:10:49.720
Don't be fooled.

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:52.810
There is only one that we're trying to rescue!

00:10:56.770 --> 00:10:58.100
That's it!

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:00.250
That's it. Our eyes met!

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:01.410
I'm certain.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:03.460
I felt destiny in our gaze!

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:05.240
You've finally found him?

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:06.690
Go, Private Arashi!

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:08.510
Arashi here, going now!

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:14.610
Private Arashi!

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:17.900
This is our last coin!

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.780
Go for it, Private Arashi.

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:21.730
Captain...

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:23.640
I'll do it.

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:33.820
This is it!

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:39.750
Why?

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:42.190
This machine's broken!

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:43.770
Arashi-san, calm down.

00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:44.940
Now, I'm mad!

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:46.380
We'll use my coins.

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:49.940
Arashi-san, you brought money?

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:54.910
Gimme your telephone number 6-7-0!

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:01.260
Hello, this is your friendly neighborhood detective agency,

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:08.020
handling everything from criminal to background investigations, with a friendly, helpful manner,

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:10.090
a constant smile, and an emphasis on speedy resolution and customer service,

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:12.800
as well as easily understood billing charges!

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:16.790
Um, there's something I'd like to ask you.

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:21.560
Go ahead. Whatever it is, we can help you.

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:24.300
Actually, something's really been bothering me lately.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:27.960
What's the difference between
tororo soba and yamakake soba?

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:29.090
Huh?

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:32.810
It's been worrying me so much, I can't even sleep at night.

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:41.200
Hello, this is your friendly neighborhood detective agency,

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:47.960
handling everything from criminal to background investigations, with a friendly, helpful manner,

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:49.940
a constant smile, and an emphasis on speedy resolution and customer service,

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:52.030
as well as easily understood billing charges!

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:54.860
Um, I'd like to ask you about something.

00:12:54.860 --> 00:12:56.190
Yes, go ahead.

00:12:56.220 --> 00:13:00.110
What's the difference between
tororo soba and yamakake soba?

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:06.980
Hello, this is your friendly neighborhood detective agency,

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:12.320
handling everything from criminal to background investigations, with a friendly, helpful manner,

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:13.990
a constant smile, and an emphasis on speedy resolution and customer service,

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:16.940
as well as easily understood billing charges!
What do you want?

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:19.100
What's the difference between-

00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:24.980
Maybe the name is too long...

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:31.050
Finally got it...

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:34.380
I didn't know you hated losing that much.

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:36.330
Quiet!

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:42.320
Here, a present for you.

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:44.580
You sure?

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:46.720
You like it, don't you, Hajime-chan?

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:49.780
Thank you.

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:52.800
That was fun.

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:58.780
Be careful. There's more to women than meets the eye.

00:14:09.730 --> 00:14:11.520
What's so funny, Hajime-chan?

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:14.080
I don't even really care anymore, somehow.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:16.480
What are you talking about?

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:17.590
Nothing.

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:19.410
It's my secret.

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:21.170
Oh, Hajime-chan...

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:32.080
Actually, I have a secret I haven't told you yet.

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:37.680
And, in fact, I'd like your help with it.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:40.510
Will you help me?

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:42.070
Help you?

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:44.780
I want you to travel with me again.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:49.570
Go back to the past with me.

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:52.810
You still don't believe I'm a ghost, do you?

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:59.830
When I connect with a boy, I can use that power to travel through time.

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:05.050
Hajime-chan, you connected with me.

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:10.150
Well, I dunno... It's all so unscientific.

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:13.170
I didn't believe it at first, either.

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:15.290
But it's real.

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:17.510
You experienced it once yourself, right?

00:15:17.510 --> 00:15:18.450
But...

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:20.260
I want you to help me.

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:22.430
Please.

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:34.580
Thank you, Hajime-chan!

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:46.150
Showa 20 (1945), January

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:47.170
What the heck? It's cold.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:49.650
It's winter here now.

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:51.820
Showa 20, January.

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:54.350
The era in which Japan fought the Greater East Asia War.

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:55.970
The Greater East Asia War?

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:58.840
World War II.

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:01.000
There's no time, so we have to hurry.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:04.960
Don't get separated, or we won't be able to return.

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:07.660
Hey... Wait, Arashi-san!

00:16:08.340 --> 00:16:09.180
We'll fight this war to the end!

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:12.330
You're Murata Sankichi-kun, right?

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:15.020
Yeah. What's up, miss?

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:18.770
You're about to go to the river with your dad, right?

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:19.720
Yeah.

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.330
We're going fishing in Tsurumi River.

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:23.310
Who are you two?

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:24.670
Oh, Dad!

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:26.700
Hello there, Murata-san.

00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:32.240
I'm Arashiyama Sayoko, from Ookurayama Women's High School.

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:35.020
I have a request for you, Murata-san.

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:36.650
What is it?

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:39.420
I'd like you not to go fishing.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:44.910
Forty minutes from now, a bombing raid will target the Tsurumigawa area.

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:47.280
You heard the warning, I'm sure.

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:50.570
Please stay away from the river. It's dangerous.

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:55.770
But you know, they play those warnings every day.
I'm sure nothing will happen today.

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:57.400
It's real this time!

00:16:57.400 --> 00:17:01.730
No! I never get to go fishing with you!

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:03.740
You're back at the factory tomorrow?

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:05.580
Please, Murata-san.

00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:08.930
You know, why isn't a girl your age conscripted?

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:10.420
What are you doing around here?

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:13.600
You from some rich family?

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:16.160
Your hair's not even tied back. What's wrong with you?

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:17.300
Go home.

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:19.730
Out of the way.

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:21.570
I haven't had a day off in a long time.

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:25.040
Murata-san, is that your only pole?

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:26.490
Y-Yeah.

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:33.230
Run!

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:36.630
Hey, wait! Damn girl!

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:38.840
Arashi-san, what are you doing?

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:40.820
Wait, you two!

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:42.320
He's pissed.

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:43.460
What do we do, Arashi-san?

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:44.360
We run away!

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:51.080
Arashi-san, what are you doing?

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:54.480
We have to get back.

00:17:56.660 --> 00:17:58.920
We have to make sure he didn't go to the river.

00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:08.130
It's all right. He's at home.

00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:09.780
OK, I'm relieved.

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:11.410
There wouldn't be enough time now.

00:18:11.810 --> 00:18:13.890
I have to give back his pole.

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:15.100
I did something bad to him.

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:16.400
Arashi-san?

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:18.890
Was he crying?

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:23.790
The kid wasn't there.

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:25.500
Hajime-chan, wait at the Ark.

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:27.470
Wait, Arashi-san! I'm coming, too!

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:30.830
What?

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:32.470
The air raid warning!

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:33.750
That's...

00:18:56.060 --> 00:18:58.110
Hurry! Don't let the fire spread!

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:57.740
Arashi-san!

00:18:58.110 --> 00:18:59.370
Buckets. Bring some buckets!{D: this section's really unattractive, but I didn't know what to do with it}

00:18:58.300 --> 00:18:59.770
Arashi-san!

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:00.770
Guys, help!

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:01.320
Is anyone hurt?

00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:08.130
It's OK. It's OK now!

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:10.500
Sankichi!

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.390
Sankichi, where are you?

00:19:12.390 --> 00:19:13.830
Mister, over here!

00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:16.410
Sankichi, are you safe?

00:19:16.410 --> 00:19:17.460
Dad!

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:21.780
Thank goodness. Are you hurt?

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:25.130
No, that girl saved me.

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:26.680
Thank you, miss.

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:29.310
How?

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:35.200
How did you know the attack was coming?

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:38.900
It's impossible for somebody to be that prescient.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:40.570
Who are you?

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.740
You're not an enemy spy, are you?

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:46.500
You bastard!

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:47.990
No, Hajime-chan!

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:49.840
Don't stop me, Arashi-san!

00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:51.210
Let me knock his lights out!

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:51.930
No!

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:52.670
But...

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:54.730
No, please.

00:19:58.360 --> 00:19:59.880
It's time to go back.

00:20:17.390 --> 00:20:19.520
I'm sorry, Hajime-chan.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:22.530
This is my secret.

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:26.220
I can't travel on my own.

00:20:27.170 --> 00:20:29.830
Maybe you can't help with this. It's dangerous.

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:42.250
Hajime-chan?

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:43.220
Of course, I can.

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:46.410
Of course, I can!

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:51.950
Thank you, Hajime-chan!

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:53.890
S-Stop it, Arashi-san!

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:55.970
I love you, Hajime-chan!

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:31.280
How are you today, Yayoi?

00:22:31.280 --> 00:22:33.790
I'm very good, Kanako.

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:35.920
I see. I'm happy to hear that.

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:39.260
I read another fascinating book.

00:22:39.260 --> 00:22:42.110
I see. And what was this fascinating book called?

00:22:42.110 --> 00:22:46.210
Well... Oh, I've forgotten the title.

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:49.080
Will you tell me what kind of story it is?

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:51.030
Yes, gladly.

00:22:53.120 --> 00:22:55.570
It is a story of youth.

00:22:55.570 --> 00:22:59.510
Summer vacation has ended, and a mysterious young boy,

00:22:59.510 --> 00:23:03.130
clad in necktie and hat, is on his way to school for the new semester's start.

00:23:03.130 --> 00:23:05.980
The boy is an expert at disguises, and he loves elephants.

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:08.420
He takes the form of his friends or of wildlife,

00:23:08.420 --> 00:23:12.650
and with his clever tricks, he makes a mockery of society, its so-called "common sense,"

00:23:12.650 --> 00:23:15.500
and the adult obsession with honor, reputation, and prestige.

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:18.510
My, what an enjoyable story.

00:23:18.510 --> 00:23:22.340
This young police sergeant had a phrase he would always use.

00:23:22.340 --> 00:23:24.810
What is it? Tell me.

00:23:27.620 --> 00:23:28.880
<i>Off with his head!</i>

00:23:31.150 --> 00:23:32.600
When you think of summer-

00:23:32.600 --> 00:23:33.800
You think of fans!

00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:34.890
No, air conditioners.

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:36.140
You have no sense of romance, Master.

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:39.560
Come on, when the master gets all sweaty, her makeup gets wrecked and sticky.

00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:41.390
I don't wear that much makeup!

00:23:41.390 --> 00:23:43.760
Get up bright and early again tomorrow!

00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:50.240
<i>Get up bright and early next time!</i>
